@@ -10,3 +10,14 @@ other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards
 refers to. It throws an `Error` if the pointer is not valid (RFC 6901 section 3) or does not resolve to a
 value of the document (section 4: missing member, out-of-range or non-canonical array index, `-`,
