+
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a JSON Patch (an array of operations)
+and returns the result as a new value; neither the document nor the patch is mutated. The six operations
+`add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test` follow RFC 6902 section 4 (`add` accepts `-` and an
+index up to the array length; `move` into one of its own children is an error; `test` compares objects
+without regard to member order). It throws an `Error` if the patch is not an array of valid operations
+(missing or ill-typed `op`, `path`, `from` or `value`, unknown `op`, invalid pointer) or if an operation
+fails; the patch is atomic (section 5), so nothing is returned on failure. Only own members are
+addressed, and `__proto__` is handled as plain data.
